window.bookSummaryJSON = "<p>Through loss comes rebirth...</p> <p>After losing someone precious to them, Gabriel has thrown himself headlong into learning magic, Florian has taken an enthusiastic apprentice under his wing, and Solomon has deepened his faith in order to grapple with an ever-changing world.</p> <p>But with a new year comes new problems, and the trees in Augarten are getting sick... even the one that has proven to be so critical to Gabriel's survival. As Gabriel himself falls ill, he digs into Florian's old journals, looking for answers to his past in the tear-soaked pages.</p> <p>Gabriel scrambles to find an answer that will save everyone he loves without losing what he has worked so hard for. The nature spirit wants Gabriel's magic and is growing impatient, but how can Gabriel relinquish it after so much has been sacrificed on its behalf?</p> <p><i>Hiraeth</i> is the third book in the Augarten series, which is best listened to in order, and is an MMM romance with magical realism, an apathetic nature spirit, lots of bicycle riding, and espresso on delivery.</p> <p>The Augarten series is now complete and is best listened to in order: <i>Equinox, Syzygy, Hiraeth, Florian, Newyddian</i> and <i>Eviternity</i>.</p>"; 
